Bilkul sahi bhai 😄 — yehi to reason hai doosra error ka:  

```
Cannot find name 'DashboardComponent'
```

TypeScript ko us class ka reference hi nahi mil raha kyunki **“DashboardComponent” naam ki class actually exist hi nahi kar rahi**.  

Chalo step‑by‑step dekhte hain tu kya kar sakta hai 👇  

---

## 🧩 Option 1: Simply Remove `DashboardComponent`
Agar tumhara goal bas services chalana aur console output dekhna hai (Angular ke bina),
to `DashboardComponent` ka koi kaam nahi.  
Tum sirf apne services aur `LoginService` ko hi use kar sakte ho.

**🧠 main.ts (simplified version)**

```typescript
import { UserService } from './services/user.service';
import { ProductService } from './services/product.service';
import { LoginService } from './services/login.service';

// services instantiate karke manually DI kar rahe hain
const user = new UserService();
const product = new ProductService();
const login = new LoginService(user);

// ab apne methods call karo
login.userLogin();

console.log('--- Summary ---');
const userInfo = user.getUserInfo();
const products = product.getProducts();

console.log(`👤 User: ${userInfo.name} (${userInfo.email})`);
console.log(`🛒 Total Products: ${products.length}`);
console.log('📦 Products:', products.map(p => p.name).join(', '));
```

✅ Isme `DashboardComponent` ki zarurat hi nahi, saara logic services se hi chal gaya.  

